      "severity": "major",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "input_field": "manuscript_text",
          "exact_quote": "directly shape the distribution of human capital",
          "location_hint": "Discussion, opening paragraph"
        },
        {
          "input_field": "manuscript_text",
          "exact_quote": "The above help us to (at least partially) refute",
          "location_hint": "Discussion, national dynamism"
        },
        {
          "input_field": "manuscript_text",
          "exact_quote": "provides a view that can be representative of the EU as a",
          "location_hint": "Methodological remarks, country selection"
        }
      ],
      "reasoning": "No regional data on GDP, sectoral composition, urbanisation, institutional quality or age structure is analysed alongside the LQs. There is no correlation, regression or systematic comparison. The determinants are drawn from the literature and illustrated with selected regions. Spillovers cannot be refuted without measuring effects on neighbouring regions over time. Five purposively chosen (ERUA-linked) countries cannot be called representative of the EU. The policy recommendations and the conclusion about vicious and virtuous cycles therefore go beyond the evidence."
    },
